  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "IFNA catches only #N/A, passes all other errors through without reading value_if_na, and shows 0 for a blank cell",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527, IFNA(value, value_if_na) evaluates value lazily and substitutes value_if_na only when value is #N/A; any other worksheet error (such as #DIV/0!) is returned unchanged without evaluating value_if_na, and a blank cell in value returns the empty value (displayed as 0 in a cell). All 4,166 full-bank IFNA rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in CalcFunc-Evidence admit2-answers-ifna-special.json (Excel 16.0 build 20527) and DnaCalc jnt_logical_info rows 93-95; 4,166/4,166 full-bank rows match.",
